email-tree.text:
A large tree in your neighbour's backyard hangs over the fence into your yard. Recently it has been causing problems for your family. You have decided to email your neighbour, Mr. Wong.

In your email:
- describe the problem;
- explain how it is affecting your family;
- suggest a solution.

Write about 150–200 words. (27 minutes)

email-course.text:
You registered and paid $120 for a ten-week evening first-aid course at a community centre in Kamloops. After two classes, the centre has moved the course from Tuesday to Thursday evenings. You work on Thursday evenings.

Write an email to the program coordinator, Ms. Bergeron. In your email:
- explain who you are and which course you registered for;
- describe why the new schedule is a problem for you;
- say what you would like the coordinator to do.

Write about 150–200 words. (27 minutes)
